                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Gameplay: 4/10[/h1]\n[h1]Graphics & Sound: 4/10[/h1]\n[h1]Narration: 6/10[/h1]\n\nThis is just a follow-up for An Assassin in Orlandes, so expect more of the same. If you enjoyed the first game, this one should suit you just fine. If you didn't, like me, well you should look elsewhere. The writing is arguably a bit better here, but overall the core remains the same, with the same oldschool awkwardness, the same UX issues, and the same repetitive and annoying background music. I managed to endure the first game until the end, but I wouldn't recommend any of those.",
